  "description": "A superb five-bedroom B-rated family home offering spacious accommodation and an enviable Glasnevin location close to every amenity.\n\nSavills is delighted to present 53A Marguerite Road, a superb five-bedroom detached family residence ideally positioned in one of Glasnevin's most established roads. Extending to approximately 133 sq m / 1,432 sq ft, this impressive B-rated home offers well-appointed accommodation, modern energy efficiency and generous living space perfectly suited to contemporary family living.\n\nBehind its attractive façade lies a bright and well-balanced interior designed to maximise both comfort and functionality. The accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall, spacious living areas, a well-equipped kitchen and dining space, five generously proportioned bedrooms and four bathrooms, providing ample flexibility for growing families, remote working or guest accommodation.\n\nThe property benefits from an excellent flow throughout, with light-filled rooms and a practical layout that caters effortlessly to everyday living and entertaining alike. The B BER rating ensures improved energy efficiency, lower running costs and enhanced year-round comfort.\n\nTo the rear, the property enjoys a spacious private garden together with a large shed that significantly enhances the home's functionality. In addition to providing excellent storage, the structure offers superb potential to be transformed into a dedicated home office or studio.\n\n53A Marguerite Road offers a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial five-bedroom family home in a mature and highly convenient location. This is a home that will appeal to a wide range of purchasers seeking both space and convenience in the heart of Glasnevin.\n\nMarguerite Road enjoys an excellent position in the heart of Glasnevin, one of Dublin's most desirable residential suburbs. The area is renowned for its mature tree-lined streets, strong community atmosphere and exceptional range of amenities. Residents are within easy reach of a selection of highly regarded primary and secondary schools, Dublin City University, the National Botanic Gardens and Griffith Park. An abundance of local shops, cafés, restaurants are nearby, while frequent bus services provide convenient access to Dublin City Centre. The M50, Dublin Airport and the surrounding business districts are also readily accessible, making this an exceptionally convenient location for families and commuters alike.",
